Node ID=90 Moral Test
Text=Kabool must test your moral judgment, to see if you are worthy of gaining the trust of the Knights of Saladin. You have been entrusted with a solemn duty to uphold the law and are ordered to investigate the murder of an old man. To your shock, you learn that your younger brother is the killer. As justification for his crime, your brother invoked the right of fair retribution - a year before, the old man killed your brother's best friend and stole from his family. What would you do?
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I would try to settle the matter with gold, paying the old man's family for their grief.
Go to node ID=120 fail
Icon=Barter Skill Icon

Requirement=Speech moreequal 90
Reply Text=I would urge my brother to turn himself, but I would strive to clear his name.
Go to node ID=110 trial 2
Icon=Speach Skill Icon

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Nothing is more important than family. I would stall the investigation and secretly help my brother escape capture.
Go to node ID=120 fail

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=My brother's actions were just. I would shield him from prosecution.
Go to node ID=120 fail

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=My brother is guilty and so must be punished. I would capture him and let justice prevail.
Go to node ID=110 trial 2

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I would change my report to make the crime look like self defense, so my brother would be guilty of a lesser crime.
Go to node ID=120 fail

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I would relieve myself of my duties to avoid the dilemma
Go to node ID=120 fail
